Installation Instructions for gkey
**********************************

Requirements
============

  * Rust 1.80 or later, with cargo
  * pkg-config
  * the TPM2 Software Stack, tpm2-tss 2.4 or later, with development
    files (tss2-esys, tss2-tctildr, tss2-mu)
  * GNU Autoconf, when building from the version control repository
  * Texinfo, to build the manual

At run time gkey needs a TPM 2.0 reachable through /dev/tpmrm0, the
uhid kernel module, systemd (for the unit, systemd-logind and
systemd-sysusers), the D-Bus system bus, polkit, and a polkit
authentication agent in each user's session.

For 'make check', swtpm is needed to run the tests that use a TPM, and
python-fido2 1.x to run the interoperability test.

Basic Installation
==================

     autoconf             # only when building from the repository
     ./configure --prefix=/usr --sysconfdir=/etc --localstatedir=/var
     make
     make check
     make install

'configure' accepts the usual options, such as '--prefix=DIR' (default
'/usr/local').  gkey-service is installed in SBINDIR and keeps its data
in LOCALSTATEDIR/lib/gkey unless systemd gives it a state directory.
In addition:

'--with-systemdsystemunitdir=DIR'
     Where to install the systemd unit (PREFIX/lib/systemd/system).

'--with-sysusersdir=DIR'
     Where to install the account definition (PREFIX/lib/sysusers.d).

'--with-udevrulesdir=DIR'
     Where to install the udev rule (PREFIX/lib/udev/rules.d).

'--with-modulesloaddir=DIR'
     Where to install the kernel module list (PREFIX/lib/modules-load.d).

'--with-polkitactiondir=DIR'
     Where to install the polkit actions (DATADIR/polkit-1/actions).

'--with-dbussystemdir=DIR'
     Where to install the D-Bus policy (DATADIR/dbus-1/system.d).

When installing under /usr/local, udev, systemd, polkit and D-Bus may
not look in the default directories; installing with '--prefix=/usr'
as shown above avoids the problem.

Run 'make' as yourself before 'sudo make install': 'make install' does
not run cargo again when the programs are up to date, but if it has to,
cargo running as root uses root's home directory and rebuilds every
dependency.

The Makefile honours DESTDIR, and provides the standard targets
'install-strip', 'uninstall', 'installcheck', 'info', 'html', 'pdf',
'dist', 'clean', 'distclean' and 'maintainer-clean'.

After installation, follow the "Setting up" chapter of the manual
('info gkey').
